<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7423" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Centrōnes</span></b> , um,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέντρωνες</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a people of Gaul.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In Gallia Narbonensis, now
				<i>Centron</i>, <i>in the valley
				Tarantaise</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 1, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 20,
				24, § 135</span></i>.—Hence, Centronicae Alpes,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				11, 42, 97, § 240</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In Gallia Belgica, near <i>Courtray</i>, acc. to Reich. <i>Thorout</i>, not far from Brügge, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G.
				5, 39</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
